From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The412Banner <the412banner@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 19:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] sechost, advapi32: Import rpcrt4 directly.

Reapplies Proton's "HACK: Avoid delay importing rpcrt4" (Billy Laws,
be454c4d1d6), which Proton reverted in 8fb9c7f7154 (Jacek Caban) once
Valve's LLVM produced correct ARM64EC exit thunks for variadic calls.
sechost and advapi32 call NdrClientCall2(), which is variadic, through a
delay import. With exit thunks that are wrong for that call, the first
service-manager request crashes.

GOG games hit it at start: Galaxy64.dll opens the service manager
(OpenSCManager over \pipe\svcctl), the call faults in rpcrt4, and DOOM
(2016) shows "The engine has crashed!". Bannerlator's layers had the same
crash and carry this change since proton-wine 5ba0fcd66f (2026-10-30).
Importing rpcrt4 directly is correct with any toolchain.

The sechost line differs from the original hack: this tree's sechost also
imports setupapi.
---
--- a/dlls/advapi32/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/advapi32/Makefile.in
@@ -1,8 +1,8 @@
 EXTRADEFS = -D_ADVAPI32_
 MODULE    = advapi32.dll
 IMPORTLIB = advapi32
-IMPORTS   = kernelbase sechost msvcrt
-DELAYIMPORTS = cryptsp rpcrt4 user32 userenv
+IMPORTS   = kernelbase sechost msvcrt rpcrt4
+DELAYIMPORTS = cryptsp user32 userenv
 
 SOURCES = \
 	advapi.c \
--- a/dlls/sechost/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/sechost/Makefile.in
@@ -1,7 +1,6 @@
 MODULE    = sechost.dll
 IMPORTLIB = sechost
-IMPORTS   = kernelbase setupapi
-DELAYIMPORTS = rpcrt4
+IMPORTS   = kernelbase setupapi rpcrt4
 
 SOURCES = \
 	plugplay.idl \
